  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Transportation obligated $9.1B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Those obligations came through 11,090 awards, with an average award size of $821K, and obligations are up 0.9% year over year. Yearly totals show a steady rise from $7B in FY21 to $9.1B in FY26, with FY22 at $8B, FY23 at $8.7B, FY24 at $8.6B, and FY25 at $9B. The largest spending categories in FY2026 to date are Engineering Services at $1.4B and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $1B, followed by Telecommunications Resellers at $917M and Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing at $567M. The agency also directs significant dollars to Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $565M and Deep Sea Freight Transportation at $559M. On the vendor side, HARRIS CORPORATION is the top recipient at $917M, followed by RAYTHEON COMPANY at $645M and ROHDE & SCHWARZ USA, INC. at $403M. This snapshot covers contract obligations only and reflects fiscal year to date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Transportation's contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations are up 0.9% year over year. Annual totals rose from $7B in FY21 to $9.1B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $8B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $8.6B in FY24, and $9B in FY25. The FY2026 to date total is $9.1B, which is the current-year partial total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do the department's contract dollars go?",
        "body": "Engineering Services leads at $1.4B, followed by Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $1B. Other top categories include Telecommunications Resellers at $917M, Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing at $567M, Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $565M, and Deep Sea Freight Transportation at $559M. The top vendors include HARRIS CORPORATION at $917M and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $645M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Transportation spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Transportation spends $9.1B on contracts in FY2026 to date. That total comes from 11,090 awards with an average award size of $821K, and obligations are up 0.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Transportation buy?",
      "a": "Transportation buys a mix of services and goods, led by Engineering Services at $1.4B and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $1B. Other major categories include Telecommunications Resellers at $917M, Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing at $567M, Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $565M, and Deep Sea Freight Transportation at $559M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Transportation's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Transportation's largest contractors are HARRIS CORPORATION at $917M, RAYTHEON COMPANY at $645M, and ROHDE & SCHWARZ USA, INC. at $403M. Other top vendors in FY2026 to date include INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. at $377M and PTSI MANAGED SERVICES INC at $275M."
